Member of operator

The member of operator is a syntax sugar syntax that enables given a context and an identifier to perform a get member operation on it for convenient access.

This allows you to do inference upon a variable declaration!

```d
Enum var = :Identifier;
```

Which is equivalent to:

```d
Enum var = __traits(getMember, Enum, "Identifier");
```

In a switch statement!

```d
switch(var) {
    case :Identifier:
        break;
}
```

Function calls:

```d
void func(Enum e) {
}

func(:Identifier);
```

Even returns:

```d
Enum func() {
    return :Identifier;
}
```

It does not support binary expressions:

```d
int var = :max - 2; // Error
```
